## Initialization and recovery

Cold construction may preset a partial `initial_vars` mapping containing control/output only. The separate `parameters` mapping uses DSL defaults for omitted parameters. Both are copied and validated. Constructor calls do not run lifecycle actions or sample inputs; the first cycle does.

<!-- example:initial-values -->

```python
machine = Device(
    sensor_values,
    initial_vars={{ example_values(model.persistent_variables.values()) }},
{% if model.parameters %}    parameters={{ example_values(model.parameters.values()) }},
{% endif %})
```

### Hot Start

The following fragment follows a successful cycle of `app.py`. Save state, all control/output values and all parameters from the same checkpoint, then construct another `Device`. The example covers a live leaf checkpoint; a composite path deliberately starts in its initial-transition wait mode. Hot start does not replay entry actions. It requires complete snapshots and is not an API for changing parameters in a running instance. A checkpoint is not a portable binary serialization format.

<!-- example:hot-start -->

```python
state = machine.current_state_path
if state is None:
    raise ValueError("Cannot restore a completed machine as a live checkpoint")
checkpoint_vars = dict(machine.vars)
checkpoint_parameters = dict(machine.parameters)
machine = Device(
    sensor_values,
    initial_state=state,
    initial_vars=checkpoint_vars,
    parameters=checkpoint_parameters,
)
```

## Results, errors and lifetime

`cycle()` returns `None`. After normal return, inspect `vars`, `current_state_path`, `is_ended` and `last_cycle_was_delta`. A Delta cycle is a successful no-progress step: persistent state holds, but the cycle consumes its input sample. `vars` contains both control and output; it is application-read-only. Each commit replaces that dictionary, so obtain it again each cycle; use `dict(machine.vars)` to retain a checkpoint. `last_inputs` and action contexts are independent read-only snapshots.

Input acquisition errors, invalid values and expression errors prevent the cycle from committing. Fix the source of the error and call `cycle()` again; readers run again. External device reads, logs and action side effects cannot be rolled back. Apply outputs to actuators after normal return when they must reflect committed state. Keep calls to a single instance serialized and do not recursively call `cycle()` from readers or hooks.

## Public API

These are the supported interfaces of the generated machine. `Device` in Quick Start is application code and forwards the full construction API. Private helpers and mutable internal storage are not integration points.

| Entry | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `{{ machine_class_name(model) }}(initial_state=None, initial_vars=None, *, parameters=None)` | Cold construction or complete hot restoration |
| `cycle(events=None, *, inputs=None)` | Execute one host-scheduled cycle; returns None |
| `vars`, `parameters`, `last_inputs` | Persistent observations, fixed configuration and last committed inputs |
| `current_state_path`, `current_state_name` | Current path tuple / short name; None after termination |
| `is_ended`, `last_cycle_was_delta`, `cycle_count` | Termination, Delta status and completed cycle count |
| `read_<input>()`, `get_input_<input>()`, `get_param_<param>()` | Implement input readers; use generated read-only getters |
| `get_abstract_hook_map()`, `ABSTRACT_HOOKS` | Mapping of DSL abstract actions to override names |
| `STATE_PATHS`, `EVENT_PATHS`, `VARIABLE_NAMES`, `DSL_SOURCE` | Generated model inventories and canonical export |
| `info()` | Diagnostic summary dictionary |

### `ReadOnlyExecutionContext`

Each action receives an independent read-only observation. Context methods below inspect that observation, without accessing live mutable storage.

| Field / method | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `vars`, `inputs`, `parameters` | Independent read-only mappings for the executing action |
| `state_path`, `active_leaf` | Executing state path; ancestor aspects report the active descendant leaf, composite enter/exit report the composite |
| `action_name`, `abstract_target` | Resolved abstract target path |
| `action_stage`, `call_stage` | Lifecycle callsite stage |
| `named_ref` | Named ref callsite, or None for direct/anonymous calls |
| `get_var(name)`, `has_var(name)` | Read/check persistent snapshot values |
| `get_state_name()`, `get_full_state_path()` | Short/full path of the executing state |

### Errors

| Error | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `NotImplementedError` | A required input reader has no implementation or explicit value |
| `ValueError` | Unknown/missing names, invalid snapshots or numeric values |
| `SimulationRuntimeExpressionError` | DSL expression evaluation failed; __cause__ preserves the numeric exception |
| `SimulationRuntimeDfsError` | Validation exceeded its structural safety limit |

Exceptions from application readers and actions propagate. Catch only failures your application can handle; report the cause before retrying. A failed cycle does not advance `cycle_count`.

